From 9941d0455a20cf3b9c8adb273b9ef595fc5d71d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JSwetz <Johnswetz1982@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:44:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): guard LinuxCNC preview measure check and catch
 spaced comment keywords

Guard the LinuxCNC probe tolerance check with the task parameter #<_task> EQ 1. In backplot preview, probe values are simulated or zero. The check stops the preview with M2 when #<_task> is not checked. With this guard, the preview continues and shows the toolpath. The tolerance check still stops the machine during live execution when #<_task> is 1.

Ignore whitespace when checking comment strings against active keywords. Add PYRELOAD to the active keyword regular expression. LinuxCNC accepts keywords with spaces and lower-case letters. The comment guard now prefixes these comments with a dash to keep them inert. Plain text like Message and Python stays unchanged.

Readings:
- LinuxCNC G-code Reference (Messages, Comments, Named Parameters #<_task>)

Pinning tests:
- crates/post/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs:
  - probe_measure_check_guarded_by_task_parameter
  - active_comment_guard_catches_spaced_keywords_and_pyreload

What was not exercised:
- Hardware execution on a physical CNC machine running LinuxCNC.

Changelog: LinuxCNC post guards probe measure check in preview mode and catches active comment keywords with spaces and PYRELOAD.

Fixes #4152
